    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-02",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Stage one has high birth and death rates, with substantial variation possible. Their average gap is small, so natural growth is slow or fluctuating. High mortality can reflect limited healthcare, poor sanitation, food insecurity or other hazards in the relevant historical setting. A high birth rate does not automatically produce rapid growth if deaths are also high. Read the difference between rates rather than the height of one line alone.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-2",
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-01-1",
