    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Stage two has a falling death rate while the birth rate remains relatively high. Improved survival opens a wider gap, increasing natural growth. The total population rises more rapidly as that positive balance accumulates. This stage illustrates why a rapid increase need not be caused by a rising birth rate: deaths can fall first. Explanations should name the survival mechanisms rather than claim that medicine alone explains every change.",
