      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Stage three has a falling birth rate alongside an already relatively low death rate. Natural increase remains positive in much of the stage but generally narrows as the rates approach. The total can continue rising, sometimes substantially, while the growth rate slows. Social opportunity, economic conditions, desired family size and access to services can contribute to the fertility change under relevant conditions.",
      "claim_ids": [
