    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-05",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Stage four has low birth and death rates, with a small natural-change gap. Growth may be slow or close to balance in the simplified model. Small differences can still produce increase or decline, and migration can alter the national total. The model's low rates do not mean births and deaths cease. A stable total can have continuing births, deaths and movement that approximately balance.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-2",
