    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-06",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A schematic four-stage rate table can use stage-one births forty and deaths thirty-eight per 1,000; stage two forty and fifteen; stage three twenty-five and ten; stage four eleven and ten. Natural increase is respectively two, twenty-five, fifteen and one per 1,000. These figures illustrate the model, not measurements of real countries. They show that the largest natural-growth gap is in the second example, not where the final population total is necessarily greatest.\n\n![Birth and death rates in four model stages with their gaps](../../assets/images/ITEM-6137-3.1-027-INTERP-answer.png)",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-2",
