    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-07",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "On a DTM chart, rates and total population need separate labels if both are shown, because they use different units. A rate curve does not become a population-count curve merely because it rises. The total can remain high after the growth rate narrows. Read axes, keys and stage boundaries before interpreting height or slope. An unlabeled line cannot support a precise calculation without knowing what it represents.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-2",
