    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-08",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A population total reflects earlier accumulation. If a stage-four population begins large and grows slowly, it may still add many people numerically. A smaller stage-two population can have a faster percentage rate and a smaller absolute increase. This distinction links the DTM to the earlier rate-versus-number examples. The stage describes component patterns, not an automatic ranking of total country size.",
      "claim_ids": [
