    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The model is a simplification, not a timetable every country follows at the same speed. Economic change, conflict, health shocks, migration and policy can alter rates or create reversals. Countries also contain varied groups and regions. A national line can hide these differences. Use the model to interpret a pattern, then recognise where real evidence requires additional explanation.",
