    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-11",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Stage identification should use both birth and death evidence. A low death rate alone could occur in several stages; the birth-rate level and direction distinguish them. Likewise, a high population total does not identify a stage. A resource answer should describe the paired rate pattern and resulting natural change before assigning the most suitable stage label.",
