    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A stage-two record with births forty and deaths fifteen per 1,000 gives twenty-five per 1,000 natural increase, or 2.5%. A stage-three record of twenty-five and ten gives fifteen per 1,000, or 1.5%. The latter is slower but still positive. If net migration is supplied separately, add it on a compatible basis to assess total change. The DTM's natural-growth calculation does not silently include it.",
