    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-13",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Population pyramids can be related to these patterns, but not assigned mechanically without context. A broad young base can be consistent with relatively high births; a narrower base can reflect lower recent births. Migration, past shocks and survival also shape the pyramid. The next sections interpret the structure directly before making a qualified link to the model.",
      "claim_ids": [
