    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-14",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The gap between two rate lines is not itself a population total. On a chart with rates per 1,000, a vertical gap of twenty represents twenty per 1,000 natural increase for that point or interval, not twenty people. To estimate a number, the relevant population denominator and period are needed. The total-population line, if present, uses its own count scale and should be read separately.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-1",
