    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-15",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A stage transition can be recognised through direction as well as level. In stage two, a relatively high birth line with a falling death line creates a widening gap. In stage three, the falling birth line narrows the gap above the low death line. Both can have a low death rate at some point, so that observation alone cannot distinguish them. Use the whole supplied pattern and key.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-1",
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-2",
