    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-16",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "The model does not claim every population had exactly equal rates at stage boundaries. Its purpose is a broad explanation of changing mortality and fertility. A small positive or negative difference at low rates can occur without changing the basic description of a late transition. If a resource includes migration or an extension beyond the four-stage model, distinguish that information from the four stages taught here rather than silently changing their meaning.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.1.06-1",
