    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-17",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Health shocks can temporarily alter mortality, while conflict or migration can affect age structure. Such events may create a short reversal not represented by a smooth teaching curve. A real time series can therefore look less orderly than a model. This does not justify forcing observations onto the curve or inventing dates when each country supposedly changed stage. Use the model as an interpretive framework with stated limitations.",
      "claim_ids": [
