    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-18",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Population momentum explains another lag. A large cohort entering childbearing ages can keep annual births substantial even if average births per woman fall. Over time the age structure adjusts, but not immediately. A graph showing a falling birth rate and a rising total can therefore be internally consistent. Check the units and accumulation before reporting a contradiction.",
