    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.1.06-19",
      "block_type": "cross_link",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A supported stage answer can be brief and precise: name the stage, describe both rates and explain the natural-growth implication. For stage two, high births and falling deaths create a wide positive gap. For stage three, falling births narrow it while the total still rises. These distinctions connect mechanism, chart reading and structure instead of treating the stages as names to memorise without interpretation.",
